@startuml line-conditions
' START, STOP, and RESET as generated by the master (docs/spec/02-line-conditions.md, section 2.2).
' A DATA change while CLK is high is a line condition: falling = START, rising = STOP.
scale 10 as 90 pixels
hide time-axis
binary "CLK" as CLK
binary "DATA" as DATA
concise "Condition" as C

@0
CLK is low
DATA is high
C is idle
@10
CLK is high
C is START
@15
DATA is low
@20
CLK is low
C is "first bit"
@23
DATA is high
@30
CLK is high
@40
CLK is low
C is "last bit"
@43
DATA is low
@50
CLK is high
@60
CLK is low
C is STOP
@70
CLK is high
@75
DATA is high
@80
CLK is low
C is idle
@100
CLK is high
C is RESET
@105
DATA is low
@110
DATA is high
@115
CLK is low
C is idle
@125
C is {-}

CLK@10 <-> @15 : T_COND
CLK@70 <-> @75 : T_COND
@enduml
